 30 crore surplus would result if exports exceeded imports by Rs 30 crore; the stem instead gives exports of 120 and imports of 150.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"contradicts_stem\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"B\",\n      \"strongest_reading\": \"A Rs 270 crore surplus would require exports to exceed imports by Rs 270 crore; the stated figures instead show imports exceed exports by Rs 30 crore.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"contradicts_stem\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"D\",\n      \"strongest_reading\": \"A Rs 270 crore deficit would require imports to exceed exports by Rs 270 crore; the stated gap is only Rs 30 crore.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"contradicts_stem\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocking_defects\": [],\n  \"style_notes\": [],\n  \"cuet_fit\": {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"syllabus_objective\": {\n        \"level\": 3,\n        \"evidence\": \"Applies the unit's named balance-of-payments surplus/deficit concept.\"\n      },\n      \"format_authenticity\": {\n        \"level\": 3,\n        \"evidence\": \"A four-option numerical MCQ in the style of the supplied authenticated economics items.\"\n      },\n      \"level_calibration\": {\n        \"level\": 2,\n        \"evidence\": \"A simple subtraction and interpretation, at the easier edge of the supplied medium numerical examples.\"\n      },\n      \"discrimination_value\": {\n        \"level\": 3,\n        \"evidence\": \"Options test sign interpretation and confusing the difference with the sum.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"reasoning_steps\": 2,\n    \"estimated_difficulty\": \"easy\",\n    \"cognitive_level\": \"application\",\n    \"exemplar_ids_compared\": [\n      \"cuet2024-economics-bookA-q2\",\n      \"cuet2024-economics-bookA-q46\",\n      \"cuet2024-economics-bookA-q50\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"option_resolution\": [\n    {\n      \"option\": \"A\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"trade surplus of Rs 30 crore\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"A country's exports of goods are Rs 120 crore and its imports of goods are Rs 150 crore.\",\n      \"reason\": \"120 − 150 = −30; imports exceed exports, so the result is a deficit, not a surplus.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"B\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"A trade surplus of Rs 270 crore\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"A country's exports of goods are Rs 120 crore and its imports of goods are Rs 150 crore.\",\n      \"reason\": \"120 − 150 = −30; the stated figures yield neither a surplus nor a Rs 270 crore balance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"C\",\n      \"status\": \"supported\",\n      \"false_part\": \"\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"A country's exports of goods are Rs 120 crore and its imports of goods are Rs 150 crore.\",\n      \"reason\": \"120 − 150 = −30; E1.1 maps negative NX with imports exceeding exports to a trade deficit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"D\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"Rs 270 crore\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"A country's exports of goods are Rs 120 crore and its imports of goods are Rs 150 crore.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The imports-minus-exports gap is Rs 30 crore, not Rs 270 crore.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
